			<div class="content" id="post-content-4156753">
									

<p>When I get anxious at home and there's nothing else for me to do, I enjoy baking. One of my favourite things to bake is shortcrust pastry, because there's a very tactile sense of satisfaction I get from actually making it. Specifically, the part where you rub the butter into the dry ingredients; where you feel the cold grease of it mixing into the flour; where you can grab a handful of the mixture and just grab it in a fist and <em>squeeze</em> and feel butter melt and ooze out between the gaps in your fingers.</p>
<p>After having read the final addendum of this piece I don't think I'll ever think about that squeezing the same way again.</p>

