<p>It’s interesting - I deliberately wrote this without trying for consistency of effects, because I wanted to play with the idea, and because three logs of the same thing would be dull.</p>
<p>It wasn’t until I finished writing the D Class test (which was the last one I wrote) that I realised that there is consistency in how the room behaves, even if the precise effects are different. I would suggest there are two possible throughlines to be found, for those who (like me) appreciate internal logic.</p>

